# Boolean formats: a `Boolean` column reads `true` and `false`, and also `1`
# and `0`, `x` and `o`, `X` and `O`. Its format, in brackets, says how it is
# shown: `10`, `xo` or `XO`, the symbol for true and then for false. The value
# is unchanged; only how it is shown. An empty cell is neither.

# The truth table of two inputs, with the gates `and`, `or`, `xor`, `nand` and
# `nor` written between the inputs. `Sum` and `Mul` are the arithmetic on 0 and 1 that they come from:
# AND is the product being 1 and XOR is the sum being 1.
sheet Truth

A    : Boolean[10]
B    : Boolean[10]
And  : Boolean[10]
Or   : Boolean[10]
Xor  : Boolean[10]
Nand : Boolean[10]
Nor  : Boolean[10]
Sum  : Integer
Mul  : Integer

| A     | B     | And | Or | Xor | Nand | Nor | Sum | Mul |
| ----- | ----- | --- | -- | --- | ---- | --- | --- | --- |
| false | false | *   | *  | *   | *    | *   | *   | *   |
| false | true  | *   | *  | *   | *    | *   | *   | *   |
| true  | false | *   | *  | *   | *    | *   | *   | *   |
| true  | true  | *   | *  | *   | *    | *   | *   | *   |

And  := A and B
Or   := A or B
Xor  := A xor B
Nand := A nand B
Nor  := A nor B
Sum  := A.Integer + B.Integer
Mul  := A.Integer * B.Integer

# Noughts and crosses: `X` is true, `O` is false and an empty square is
# neither, so a line of three is won by X when all three are true and by O
# when none is.
sheet Board

A : Boolean[XO]
B : Boolean[XO]
C : Boolean[XO]

| Row | A | B | C |
| --- | - | - | - |
| 1   | X | O | X |
| 2   | O | X | O |
| 3   | O | X | X |

sheet Lines

Line : String
X    : Boolean[10]
O    : Boolean[10]

| Line     | X | O |
| -------- | - | - |
| Row 1    | = (Board[A; 0] and Board[B; 0] and Board[C; 0]) // false | = (not Board[A; 0] and not Board[B; 0] and not Board[C; 0]) // false |
| Row 2    | = (Board[A; 1] and Board[B; 1] and Board[C; 1]) // false | = (not Board[A; 1] and not Board[B; 1] and not Board[C; 1]) // false |
| Row 3    | = (Board[A; 2] and Board[B; 2] and Board[C; 2]) // false | = (not Board[A; 2] and not Board[B; 2] and not Board[C; 2]) // false |
| Column A | = Board.A.count() == 3 and Board.A.all() | = Board.A.count() == 3 and Board.A.none() |
| Column B | = Board.B.count() == 3 and Board.B.all() | = Board.B.count() == 3 and Board.B.none() |
| Column C | = Board.C.count() == 3 and Board.C.all() | = Board.C.count() == 3 and Board.C.none() |
| Diagonal | = (Board[A; 0] and Board[B; 1] and Board[C; 2]) // false | = (not Board[A; 0] and not Board[B; 1] and not Board[C; 2]) // false |
| Reverse  | = (Board[C; 0] and Board[B; 1] and Board[A; 2]) // false | = (not Board[C; 0] and not Board[B; 1] and not Board[A; 2]) // false |

sheet Result

| Winner                                                                                    |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| = if Lines.X.Integer.sum() > 0 then 'X' else if Lines.O.Integer.sum() > 0 then 'O' else 'no one yet' |

# Any two characters will do, and the column reads them back.
sheet Checklist

Done : Boolean[✓✗]

| Task  | Done |
| ----- | ---- |
| Write | ✓    |
| Test  | ✓    |
| Ship  | ✗    |
